/-!
# Content ideals over a valuation ring

Let `A → B` be a local ring map of local rings which is essentially of finite type and let `N`
be a finite `B`-module which is flat as an `A`-module. If `A` is a valuation ring, then every
element of `N` has a content ideal `I ⊆ A` in the sense of Stacks 0ASA, and `I` is principal.

## Main results

* `IsContentIdeal.isPrincipal_of_valuationRing`: a content ideal of an element of a module over
  a valuation ring is a principal ideal. This is the second assertion of Stacks 0ASX, and it
  needs none of the geometric hypotheses: a content ideal is finitely generated (Stacks 0ASB)
  and a valuation ring is Bézout, so every finitely generated ideal is principal
  (Stacks 090Q).

Both assertions of Stacks 0ASX together are
`exists_isContentIdeal_isPrincipal_of_valuationRing_of_flat` in
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Valuation/ContentIdealExistence.lean`.

